{
  "A one-line text field with its label, help text and error: placeholder, prefix and suffix, buttons in the box, a clear button, a password that can be shown, a character counter, an input mask and validation — alone, in a group, or every field in a panel.": "",
  "Every prop takes a value or a function; a function of a reactive object keeps the field in step with it. `x-model` binds the value two-way. Created with `new`, the same properties are set programmatically.": "",
  "The label goes above the box, next to it (`side`), inside it until there is a value (`floating`), or only to screen readers (`hidden`). `&` marks its access key.": "",
  "Prefix, suffix, icon, buttons": "",
  "`prefix` and `suffix` are fixed text around the value; `icon` sits at the start; `buttons` adds your own, each with its own `enabled`, `visible` and `position`.": "",
  "Password, counter": "",
  "Mask": "",
  "A mask keeps the text in shape while it is typed, deleted or pasted; the caret skips the fixed characters. The value is the typed characters only, or with `maskValue=\"formatted\"` the text as shown. A mask that is not filled in fails validation.": "",
  "Character": "",
  "A digit.": "",
  "A digit that may stay empty.": "",
  "A letter.": "",
  "A letter or a digit.": "",
  "The next character is fixed: `\\\\0` is a fixed zero.": "",
  "A fixed character, skipped while typing.": "",
  "Validation": "",
  "A field checks itself when it is left after a change, then on every change until the value passes. `required`, `minLength`, `type=\"email\"` and a mask bring their own rules; `rules` adds yours, async ones too. `error` shows a message from outside, e.g. from the server.": "",
  "Without a group, `validateFields(panel)` checks every field inside a component or an element: a panel, a dialog, a page.": "",
  "Commits the value (with `updateOn=\"change\"`) and fires `onEnter`.": "",
  "The buttons you add and the password button are Tab stops; the clear button is not (Escape does its job).": "",
  "A native `<input>`; its `<label>` is tied to it with `for`.": "",
  "`aria-invalid=\"true\"`; the message line is a polite live region, so a new error is read out.": "",
  "The clear and password buttons are named from `uiLocale`; the password button has `aria-pressed`.": "",
  "The names of the clear and password buttons and every validation message come from `uiLocale.strings`; every field follows a change at once, errors already shown included.": "",
  "The field. `data-size`, `data-variant`, `data-label-mode`, `data-invalid`, `data-readonly`, `data-disabled`, `data-filled`, `data-required`, `data-stretch`.": "",
  "Added by TextBox.": "",
  "The label, the box, the input.": "",
  "The parts at the sides of the input.": "",
  "The width when not stretched.": "",
  "Units: the box, a state layer over its fill, the frame (with `frame-start`, `frame-notch`, `frame-end` around a notch), the line along its bottom and a ring under the keys, each with its box per state: per variant (`filled-…`, `underline-…`), status (`invalid`, `readonly`, `disabled`) and `hover`, `focus`, `pressed`.": "",
  "Units: the label (`focus`, `invalid`, `disabled`, `floating-…`), the required mark and the parts beside the text.": "",
  "Units: the groups of buttons in the box, the buttons (`hover`, `pressed`, `focus`, `disabled`) and what they show.": "",
  "Units: the line under the box (`shown`, `invalid`, `disabled`), the help or error text and the counter.": "",
  "The frame’s width, spacing and the label.": "",
  "Icons, and how far the buttons sit from the box’s edges.": "",
  "The floating label and the notch cut for it.": "",
  "The text. `x-model` binds it two-way.": "",
  "`top`, `side` (next to the box), `floating` (inside the box until there is a value), `hidden` (only for screen readers).": "",
  "A line under the box. An error message takes its place.": "",
  "`text`, `password`, `email`, `search`, `tel`, `url`. `email` and `url` also check the format.": "",
  "Fixed text before / after the value inside the box (`https://`, `kg`).": "",
  "An icon at the start of the box.": "",
  "Buttons of your own inside the box, at the start or the end.": "",
  "With `type=\"password\"`: a button that shows the password.": "",
  "Limits; `minLength` is checked by validation.": "",
  "`12/50` under the box (`12` without `maxLength`).": "",
  "`change`: the value changes when the field is left or Enter is pressed.": "",
  "Can be read, selected and copied, not changed.": "",
  "A mark after the label, `aria-required`, and a `required` rule.": "",
  "See Mask.": "",
  "Mask characters of your own.": "",
  "Shown in the places not filled yet.": "",
  "`raw`: only the typed characters; `formatted`: with the fixed ones.": "",
  "`focus`: an empty mask shows only while the field has focus.": "",
  "See Validation.": "",
  "An error from outside (the server); shown until cleared.": "",
  "The group it is checked with.": "",
  "A value or a function, like the prop: `box.error = () => this.model.nameError` is followed.": "",
  "`false` while an error shows.": "",
  "The error shown, `''` without one.": "",
  "An asynchronous rule is running.": "",
  "Every place of the mask is filled.": "",
  "Your `buttons` may be plain or reactive; the field reads them as they are. After changing them in place, call `refresh()`. Every editor has it; a list editor reads its items again too.": "",
  "The value changed. `e`: `{ value, previousValue, byUser, source, event? }`; `byUser` tells the user programmatically.": "",
  "Checks": "",
  "Something must be entered.": "",
  "An email address / a web address.": "",
  "A `RegExp`, or a string that must match the whole value (like the HTML `pattern`).": "",
  "The number of characters.": "",
  "A number or a date between bounds.": "",
  "Equal to another value (a repeated password), or different with `not`.": "",
  "`check(value)` returns `true`, `false` or a message, or a promise of one (a server call).": "",
  "`message` (a value or a function) and `enabled`. Empty values pass every rule but `required` and `compare`.": "",
  "The frame (`Field`), the mask (`InputMask`, which works on any `<input>`) and validation (`ValidationGroup`, `validateFields`, `checkRules`) are shared parts, exported for other components and your own.": ""
}
